From: SM-A105F Linux 6.18.54 board port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: reserve fixed A10 memory regions

Carry forward the exact fixed physical ranges declared by the Samsung 4.4.177
Exynos7885/A10 memory sources. The standard reserved-memory reg entries keep
these ranges out of ordinary Linux allocation. The separate memreserve entry
is retained as supplied.

Do not copy vendor ION/secure compatibles or attach consumers: their Linux
6.18 semantics are not mapped. Dynamic pools are also omitted. No no-map or
reusable property is inferred from the vendor driver's naming.

Validated against Linux 6.18.54 commit 1b357ecb321392158d507b04672ffee57bfa071d.
The A10 DTB built with CHECK_DTBS=y and the reserved-memory binding check
passed. Direct dt-validate reported the existing A10 root-compatible and
osc-clock fixed-clock issues, with no reserved-memory diagnostics. The DTB
SHA-256 is ea5b3131cfa55e02472d6f74815082282f0e3b8940471311545e558d380905b7.
This is host-side source/schema evidence only.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885-a10.dts | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885-a10.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885-a10.dts
index 000000000000..000000000000 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885-a10.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7885-a10.dts
@@ -3,5 +3,6 @@
#include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
#include <dt-bindings/input/input.h>
+/memreserve/ 0xe0000000 0xd00000;
#include "exynos7885.dtsi"

/ {
@@ -13,1 +14,17 @@
-	aliases {
+	reserved-memory {
+		#address-cells = <2>;
+		#size-cells = <1>;
+		ranges;
+
+		sec-debug@80000000 { reg = <0x0 0x80000000 0x1000>; };
+		tima@b8000000 { reg = <0x0 0xb8000000 0x200000>; };
+		seclog@c0000000 { reg = <0x0 0xc0000000 0x80000>; };
+		wifibt@e9000000 { reg = <0x0 0xe9000000 0x400000>; };
+		abox@e9400000 { reg = <0x0 0xe9400000 0x400000>; };
+		framebuffer@ec000000 { reg = <0x0 0xec000000 0x1400000>; };
+		modem@f5400000 { reg = <0x0 0xf5400000 0x8800000>; };
+		cp-ram-logging@fdc00000 { reg = <0x0 0xfdc00000 0x2000000>; };
+		gnss@ffc00000 { reg = <0x0 0xffc00000 0x400000>; };
+	};
+
+	aliases {
